			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848770">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Drama/Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> I plan to use the traditional SCP format with an ACS header. The plot will reveal itself through the recovery log and a set of phone calls received by the object.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> In the 1968 the Foundation incepted a package from one of their mailrooms. The package contained a 1940’s rotary dial telephone that receives a phone call every day at 12:00 AM despite the cord being cut. The same phone call is repeated nightly until it is changed by the caller. The phone calls slowly reveal the story of a foundation researcher who has been captured by the Chaos Insurgency. He intended to send the phone to his family in hopes to ensure them that he is safe.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The calls the man makes to his family slowly reveal a story. In the first call he will inform his family that “the guys at work” have a job for him and that he won’t be home for a little while. In the second phone call the man is less optimistic, however his tone is still hopeful and he attempts to ensure his wife that he will be home soon. He refers to his captures as “they”. In the final phone calls he refers to his captures as the Insurgency (Chaos Insurgency) and is mostly pessimistic in tone. In the final phone call, he apologizes to his family and is ill. These phone calls will take place over the course of 50 years.</p>
<p>An addendum at the end of the article will state that the foundation visited the home address that the man sent the package to. House was empty and it is implied that the family living there was killed by the Chaos Insurgency. This is meant to get an emotional response out of the reader. Not only were his calls not received by his family, but rather the foundation, but his family may not have been alive this entire time.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This article will stand out because of its extremely simple concept that requires emotional investment. It is easy for any reader to understand (you do not even need to know what the Chaos Insurgency is to understand the basic premise). It is meant to be a refreshing break from the more complex articles on the site.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The following information will be given during the article:<br />
1. No phone calls can be made on the phone. It functions as a normal, disconnected phone when not receiving its nightly call.<br />
2. The object is classified as neutralized, as it no longer makes calls.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

